He's fully, if he loses the 2020 election
is growing and it includes at least one Republican

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.559
candidate now who happens to be running against
Donald Trump.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:16.039
His name's William Weld.

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:18.710
He is a former governor here in Massachusetts.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.220
He previously was running as a libertarian.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:28.650
He now is a Republican and he says that Donald
Trump will not leave voluntarily if he loses

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.119
the 2020 election from real time with Bill
Maher.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:35.969
Bill Maher asked if Trump loses, do you think
he'll leave?

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.879
And William Weld said, not voluntarily.

00:00:37.879 --> 00:00:41.339
He'll have a run at saying it was a rigged
game, so I'm not leaving.

00:00:41.339 --> 00:00:46.050
I don't think the military and indeed even
the Justice Department, the rank and file,

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:50.719
the investigative agencies would stand for
that in this country.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:55.859
I like that William Weld added that last piece
because it's important for us on the Left

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:59.789
and not that William Weld is on the left,
but for anyone on the left who is even entertaining

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:04.379
this idea of what would Trump do, what did
he try to hold on to control if he lost the

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:05.960
2020 election?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.670
We're not like the crazy right with the birther
stuff and the Obama's going to cancel the

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:16.149
2016 election stuff, which is why I think
it's important to point out that William Weld

00:01:16.149 --> 00:01:19.200
is not saying Trump would succeed at staying
in the White House.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.320
Even if you lost the 2020 election.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:28.170
He might try to pull it or try to delay it,
but ultimately the centers of power in the

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.361
country wouldn't allow it.

00:01:29.361 --> 00:01:33.000
And I also think that that's the most likely
scenario and every single time that this comes

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.570
up, I go out of my way not to be hyperbolic,
because with Obama there was so much nonsense

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.210
about Obama won't leave.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:46.640
Obama will cancel the 2016 election and declare
himself indefinite president or Obama will

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:52.479
declare martial law as a justification for
remaining president beyond his eight years.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:56.630
We want to be a sober and realistic as possible
